  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Minor in Geographic Analysis"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Minors",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Minors",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "The Geographic Analysis Minor provides interested students with a course of study that focuses on development of real-world solutions to issues surrounding urban growth, economic development, business/service location decisions, climate change, and environmental remediation. In addition to foundation courses in location principles and exploration of the earth and ecosystems, the curriculum includes such electives as Geographic Information Systems (GIS), Geographic Data and Mapping, Demography, and Geodemographics. The minor aims to enhance the professional careers of the students in other disciplines such as Business Management, Hospitality and Tourism Management, Urban and Regional Planning, Environmental and Urban Sustainability and other programs within the Faculty of Arts."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Administered by: Department of Geography and Environmental Studies"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Exclusions: This minor is not available to students in the following programs:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Geographic Analysis",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Geographic Analysis",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/programs/arts/geographic/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Students may only pursue one of Geography or Geographic Analysis minor, double minors in Geography and Geographic Analysis will not be granted.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Geography",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/minors/geography_minor/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "To receive this Minor, students must complete six (6) courses from the following curriculum:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "One (1) required course:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "GEO 151 Location, Location, Location or PLG 300 Theories in Urban and Regional Planning",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "GEO 151",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/geography/GEO/151/"
        },
        {
          "text": "PLG 300",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/planning/PLG/300/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Plus one (1) of the following:"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "GEO 581 GIS, Geographic Data and Mapping",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "GEO 581",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/calendar/2026-2027/courses/geography/GEO/581/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
